The lousy union will say anything about a boss who won't say anything.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:18.470
Why let him get away with it? What rights he got to excuse?

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.170
Will you do me a favor? Keep out of this.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.410
This is your first day in the shop. Learn what you have to. This is none of your business.

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:25.450
Still the same.

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:27.740
What's still the same?

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:29.970
When did you ever talk anything out with me?

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:41.960
Remember, above all, Roxton desires to give you the ultimate in fashion at a price.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.700
Okay, will he bring the wire?

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:18.260
Right.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:20.660
Mr. Banana?

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:25.020
Hey, nine months old and already she's picking up the boys.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.120
I'm Alan Mitchell.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.860
Maria, shake the man's hand.

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:29.950
I want...

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.550
Say hello. Come on, baby.

00:19:34.190 --> 00:19:36.750
Look, I'm not running for president.

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:40.290
You know, in this country, everybody's got a chance.

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:44.190
Even a boss's son.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:47.000
I came by to ask you about it.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:50.740
There she goes again.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.740
What's the matter? The faucet's always on?

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.210
Okay, okay, I got the message.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.010
You know, you women are all alike.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:19:59.830
Nag, nag.

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.990
Today in the shop. What did you mean about Mr. Kenner?

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.130
What do you figure?

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.820
If I knew, I wouldn't be here.

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:11.820
You know why your old man's partner got it. What do you really want?

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.040
You mean it wasn't an accident?

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.680
Come on, get to it, will you? You're here to make a deal with the union to lay off?

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:21.590
Deal? I don't know what you're talking about.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.380
Look, I didn't come here to take dancing lessons.

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:42.130
Tonight, sir!

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:48.330
How about that spaghetti bend?

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:49.710
You don't work hard enough, old Davey,

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:50.810
beside taking care of the baby.

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:52.950
Comes Wednesday night, she's got to knock herself out

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:54.710
teaching these moms us how to dance Spanish.

00:20:59.240 --> 00:20:59.880
Tonight, sir!

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.220
change the bikini.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:27.060
They wear out their own wives.

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:35.000
She's my wife. She picked me.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:38.840
How about that? Maybe I got something. Who knows?

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.220
Come on, let's have it.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:44.580
What makes you think Mr. Kenner was murdered?

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:48.820
That's the wise guy who sent you.

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:49.640
The wise guy?

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:52.540
Your old man's hidden partner. Why don't you tell that killer he's got his payroll?

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:53.480
What did you say?

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.930
Oh, my father was right. The union will spread around anything because he won't die.

00:21:56.930 --> 00:21:58.310
Don't kid me. I don't know what's going on.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:21:59.970
And don't tell me my father's in business with...

00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:06.140
You're on a level.

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:10.360
Well, you sure got a lot to learn.

00:22:12.690 --> 00:22:14.620
Look, what I want to know is this.

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:17.120
Not now.

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:23.640
Oh, bellezza.

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:24.500
Great timing.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:25.580
I just changed it.

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:26.280
Bravo!

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:29.240
Maria, she needs a papa who's a first-class dry cleaner.

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:29.980
Now, momma...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:38.860
needs another baby to keep the way she belongs who's stopping you all the time in the middle

00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:55.890
of no matter what i'm the kid would you please oh yeah come on let's get some air hey who's

00:22:55.890 --> 00:22:59.440
your good-looking friend oh he's here on business business

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:03.980
What kind of business? You're my business.

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:04.780
Keep out of it.

00:23:05.290 --> 00:23:08.370
Listen, if it's to help organize those non-uni shop, get somebody else.

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:10.400
Tulia's done enough. Leave him out of it.

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:11.630
Well, that's not why I'm here.

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:12.820
What for, then?

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:14.020
I said keep out of it.

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:15.440
Why should I keep out of it?

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:18.370
I'm his wife. What do you want with him?

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:20.520
Mrs. Renata, I'm Alan Mitchell.

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:23.220
Mitchell? Rockstone Fashion Mitchell?

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:24.380
The son, not the boss.

00:23:24.520 --> 00:23:26.860
Anybody from that inferno, that no good.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.280
You went there after all I said.

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:29.960
Honest to people.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.780
Peter and Paul, I'm married to a crazy lunatic.

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.540
You want to be a hero for the union?

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:35.220
Go organize the devils in hell.

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:35.600
Okay.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:38.180
Listen, listen, listen, both of you.

00:23:38.570 --> 00:23:40.130
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:41.640
No, you've got to believe me.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.730
I've been out of the country for years.

00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:44.710
I just got back.

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:47.200
This is all new to me, the dress business,

00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:49.300
the stuff about the unions and the hoodlums.

00:23:49.700 --> 00:23:51.200
Don't you understand why I'm here?

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:53.480
You said things about my father.

00:24:04.220 --> 00:24:09.270
Mr. Mitchell, would you like some beer?

00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:13.420
Don't ask. Get him.

00:24:24.450 --> 00:24:26.050
Not about a minute. Cigarette?

00:24:30.890 --> 00:24:31.610
Ever hear of the edge?

00:24:32.810 --> 00:24:33.550
It's the edge.

00:24:36.710 --> 00:24:38.090
You take any union shop.

00:24:38.820 --> 00:24:41.160
They gotta pay scale, plus workers' benefits.

00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:44.200
But in a protected joint where they keep the union out,

00:24:44.600 --> 00:24:46.450
there's no minimum, no benefits.

00:24:46.940 --> 00:24:47.840
That's the edge.

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:49.640
The difference in the cost of labor.

00:24:49.880 --> 00:24:53.810
In Roxton fashions, it adds up to over half a million a year.

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:56.240
You mean my father is using...

00:24:56.240 --> 00:24:57.060
Artie Ravage.

00:24:57.990 --> 00:24:59.970
That's who your father's using to keep the union out.

00:25:00.090 --> 00:25:01.720
Who is ravaged?

00:25:02.130 --> 00:25:04.210
Everything for the needle tree, that's ravaged.

00:25:05.100 --> 00:25:07.280
Especially broken heads, acid in the face.

00:25:07.460 --> 00:25:08.260
Don't think I don't know.

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:09.140
So who asked you?

00:25:09.200 --> 00:25:11.800
Yes, and you had to get mixed up with the number one murderer.

00:25:11.900 --> 00:25:12.660
It's time you went home.

00:25:12.740 --> 00:25:15.400
Yes, every time I talk sense, it's in a mind the kid or go home.

00:25:16.010 --> 00:25:17.150
You can do me a big favor.

00:25:17.190 --> 00:25:18.990
If he comes into your place, kick him out for me.

00:25:19.050 --> 00:25:20.970
Hey, Theresa, you want it on the phone?

00:25:21.170 --> 00:25:23.850
I want a husband, not someone who's 100% union.

00:25:24.880 --> 00:25:25.880
So answer the phone.

00:25:26.120 --> 00:25:27.200
Yes, answer the phone.

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:28.320
Answer the phone.

00:25:33.290 --> 00:25:37.650
Believe it. I just can't believe my father could get mixed up with hoodlums.

00:25:38.900 --> 00:25:47.160
Dear, I understand he's your father.

00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:51.770
But when a hoodlum climbs on a manufacturer's back, it's tough to shake him off.

00:25:51.810 --> 00:25:54.950
But he couldn't have had anything to do with killing his partner. I'm sure of it.

00:25:54.990 --> 00:25:59.970
I'm not saying he did. All I know is that after I had Kenner all...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:13.880
set the sign with the union down he went 27 floors non-stop so what's the

00:26:13.880 --> 00:26:18.310
matter that call they said tell your husband to stay away from Rockstone

00:26:18.310 --> 00:26:25.290
fashion you'd be a widow that's what I mean

00:26:32.360 --> 00:26:32.920
See you later.

00:26:33.280 --> 00:26:33.820
Where are you going?

00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:34.980
I told you, I got a meeting.

00:26:35.750 --> 00:26:37.550
You mean you're still going even after the call?

00:26:37.590 --> 00:26:38.610
Who's afraid of a call?

00:26:38.910 --> 00:26:39.770
I beg you.

00:26:39.970 --> 00:26:42.170
Come on now, don't give it an offer, I'm late as it is.

00:26:45.480 --> 00:26:46.380
No, Tulio.

00:27:06.270 --> 00:27:07.690
Try not to worry, Mrs. Renata.

00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:09.260
I'll see what I can do.

00:27:12.570 --> 00:27:14.610
I can talk my father into signing with you.

00:27:16.940 --> 00:27:18.420
It's an old story in the garment jungle.

00:27:19.300 --> 00:27:20.800
It isn't only Rockstone fashion.

00:27:21.410 --> 00:27:22.770
It just happened to you picked the toughest.

00:27:24.570 --> 00:27:25.670
It's not your father's place.

00:27:25.670 --> 00:27:27.310
It'll be another, and then another.

00:27:29.590 --> 00:27:29.970
Will you once...

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:35.750
stop until every shop is organized it means that much to him he's not in it for himself

00:27:35.750 --> 00:27:43.860
to help others quite a guy yes he's quite a guy when he believes in something there's

00:27:43.860 --> 00:27:55.290
no stopping him you believe in the union too he's good of course good and bad in everything

00:28:00.090 --> 00:28:16.880
pleasure talking to you, Mrs. Renato. Teresa is my name. Teresa. Good night. Mr. Mitchell. Nice to

00:28:16.880 --> 00:28:28.640
talk to you, too. Good night. Bye.

00:28:30.190 --> 00:28:35.840
Thought so? Miller? Alfredi?

00:28:36.020 --> 00:28:36.840
What's it all about?

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:37.780
Search me.

00:28:38.040 --> 00:28:39.880
Mr. Bronson calls it. There must be a reason.

00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:40.780
But at night?

00:28:41.440 --> 00:28:42.240
At night?

00:28:44.970 --> 00:28:45.370
Turio.

00:28:47.630 --> 00:28:49.250
What's the matter, Teresa, giving you a rough time?

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:51.130
Like another union meeting, stay at home with me better?

00:28:51.310 --> 00:28:51.950
I do guess.

00:28:52.460 --> 00:28:53.880
I got a wife too, you know.

00:28:54.180 --> 00:28:56.160
Besides, whoever knew you to come late to a union meeting.

00:28:56.440 --> 00:28:58.200
Just in time.

00:29:01.020 --> 00:29:02.020
All here, Mr. Bronson.

00:29:02.700 --> 00:29:05.020
I called this secret meeting of the organizing committee

00:29:05.020 --> 00:29:06.480
as soon as I received this telegram.

00:29:07.660 --> 00:29:09.520
It's from the Manufacturers Association.

00:29:11.030 --> 00:29:13.290
Now, we've got to sign up every shop

00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:16.560
or the union shops will all pull out.

00:29:17.500 --> 00:29:20.260
Now, I don't have to remind you that 10% of the shops

00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:22.100
in the garment center are still non-union.

00:29:23.150 --> 00:29:25.190
Now, we've either got to get them in

00:29:25.190 --> 00:29:27.000
or there'll be no more.

00:29:30.440 --> 00:29:31.180
But who are these men?

00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:33.180
They're hoods.

00:29:33.950 --> 00:29:37.480
What a lousy thing to say, but so lousy.

00:29:37.980 --> 00:29:41.080
We're here to give your boys protection, Mr. Union Manager.

00:29:41.300 --> 00:29:44.160
With you to protect us, we can get measured for coffins right now.

00:29:44.380 --> 00:29:46.040
I know you're good, you flannel-mouthed punk.

00:29:46.060 --> 00:29:48.160
Any wise guy wants a pistolero calls you.

00:29:48.880 --> 00:29:49.820
Price just doubled.

00:29:50.250 --> 00:29:51.970
You need more protection than I thought.

00:29:52.110 --> 00:29:53.650
Crawl out with the rest of the lice!

00:29:56.130 --> 00:29:57.530
You spick bum.

00:29:58.320 --> 00:29:58.820
That's enough.

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:01.780
Now, get out of here. I'll call the police.

00:30:03.030 --> 00:30:03.730
Here's change.

00:30:14.260 --> 00:30:15.600
How come they know about this, mate?

00:30:16.190 --> 00:30:17.390
I'm asking how come.

00:30:18.200 --> 00:30:20.580
Because somebody here is wide direct to these goons.

00:30:21.910 --> 00:30:22.690
That's how come.

00:30:23.460 --> 00:30:27.910
Yes, I know there are traitors here in my own committee.

00:30:30.670 --> 00:30:33.670
But I want them and those they invited to hear your answer.

00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:39.360
Will you let chiselers protected by hoodlums kill your union?

00:30:39.680 --> 00:30:40.140
No!

00:30:40.890 --> 00:30:45.410
Will you bring all shops into the union and so raise the welfare of every worker in the garment industry?

00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:45.690
Yes!

00:30:46.430 --> 00:30:47.190
That is your answer?

00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:47.470
Yes!

00:30:49.200 --> 00:30:50.400
You heard our answer.

00:30:50.740 --> 00:30:51.480
And here's our.

00:30:56.840 --> 00:30:57.180
Julio!

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:05.720
Our answer is still the same.

00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:08.370
No more protected shops.

00:31:09.940 --> 00:31:11.740
Such a lousy thing to say.

00:31:12.870 --> 00:31:28.080
The middle of the season, the union's got to start another drive.

00:31:28.340 --> 00:31:29.980
Don't worry, your shop, they won't...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.920
I guarantee if you have any trouble day or night, follow me.

00:31:35.930 --> 00:31:36.850
It's heat.

00:31:37.660 --> 00:31:40.380
We pour like a regular sprinkler system.

00:31:41.050 --> 00:31:41.310
Mitchell?

00:31:42.320 --> 00:31:42.700
Yes?

00:31:42.940 --> 00:31:44.680
What about lot 472?

00:31:44.930 --> 00:31:45.690
Check with Tony.

00:31:46.850 --> 00:31:47.970
Dad, I'd like to talk to you.

00:31:48.420 --> 00:31:48.820
Malone.

00:31:49.020 --> 00:31:50.100
I'm busy now.

00:31:50.470 --> 00:31:51.190
This is important.

00:31:51.450 --> 00:31:52.410
I said I'm busy.

00:31:52.660 --> 00:31:53.340
This your son?

00:31:54.420 --> 00:31:56.080
Yes, I'll be through in a few minutes.

00:31:57.940 --> 00:31:58.540
Well, wait a minute.

00:31:58.850 --> 00:31:59.970
I'd like to meet the young...

00:32:05.100 --> 00:32:06.860
I've heard all about you, Mr. Ravage.

00:32:07.310 --> 00:32:09.940
I've heard about you, too. Your father says you're coming in the business.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:10.800
That's right.

00:32:11.960 --> 00:32:13.680
Well, you and I got a lot to talk about.

00:32:14.350 --> 00:32:15.210
Not if I can help it.

00:32:17.140 --> 00:32:19.020
Mr. Ravage is a friend of the firm.

00:32:19.670 --> 00:32:24.850
So I've been told. Everything for the needle trade, including broken heads.

00:32:25.780 --> 00:32:26.580
Who says?

00:32:28.720 --> 00:32:29.840
You wouldn't talk to me yesterday.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:36.410
So I went to the union I heard you went to the union behind my back

00:32:36.410 --> 00:32:39.910
I wanted to find out what was going on. I couldn't believe what they were saying

00:32:39.910 --> 00:32:45.620
But now I know there must be something to it. You're taking their side against mine my own son

00:32:45.620 --> 00:32:47.460
I'm not taking any sides

00:32:47.460 --> 00:32:52.040
But when you start hiring thugs to beat people up and threaten to kill them just a minute

00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:58.480
Protection's my business. That's all I give your father and nobody gets hurt unless he asks for it

00:33:00.700 --> 00:33:01.460
Is that what you think?

00:33:13.370 --> 00:33:17.320
He was at a union meeting last night

00:33:17.320 --> 00:33:18.600
when they broke in and beat him up.

00:33:19.090 --> 00:33:20.810
And before that, they told his wife they'd kill him

00:33:20.810 --> 00:33:21.990
if he didn't stay away from here.

00:33:22.270 --> 00:33:23.610
So let him stay away.

00:33:24.180 --> 00:33:27.000
You crawl back in the sewer where you belong, you dirty.

00:33:27.680 --> 00:33:29.970
You spick bum, you open your...

00:33:30.320 --> 00:33:32.160
to me and they'll carry you out of here.

00:33:32.980 --> 00:33:44.120
That's enough. Mitchell, I came here because

00:33:44.120 --> 00:33:48.140
your son asked me to. But I'm telling you

00:33:48.900 --> 00:33:50.860
we're going to bring Roxton Fashions into

00:33:50.860 --> 00:33:53.230
the union and this time nothing's going to

00:33:53.230 --> 00:33:55.600
stop us. And I'm telling you I'll

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:57.600
never go union even if I have to close

00:33:57.600 --> 00:33:59.640
my door. Well, that's just what you're going to have to do.

00:33:59.760 --> 00:33:59.960
We got

00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:02.040
truckers with us. They won't go through

00:34:02.040 --> 00:34:04.500
no picket line. Nothing will move in or out of

00:34:04.500 --> 00:34:06.540
your place if you don't sign. He'll sign

00:34:06.540 --> 00:34:08.740
for your funeral. You kill me.

00:34:09.180 --> 00:34:10.880
There are 400,000 others that take

00:34:10.880 --> 00:34:13.000
my place. I'm warning you, this is your last

00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:15.520
chance. Don't you threaten me.

00:34:16.130 --> 00:34:17.790
I'm not some little cloak and

00:34:17.790 --> 00:34:19.570
suitor you can push around. You're dealing with

00:34:19.570 --> 00:34:21.590
Walter Mitchell. Tell your union

00:34:21.590 --> 00:34:23.610
bosses they couldn't lick me before and they won't

00:34:23.610 --> 00:34:25.490
now. Dad, will you listen to reason?

00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:39.720
I told you it wouldn't do any good. Thanks for the try.

00:34:45.020 --> 00:34:47.240
Tell your hoods that they want me. They'll find me on a picket line.

00:34:55.880 --> 00:34:56.940
No troublemaker, that one.

00:34:57.140 --> 00:34:59.200
Don't you worry. The stuff will move. It'll move.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:03.040
When I get done with him, he won't bother us no more.

00:35:03.360 --> 00:35:04.160
What are you gonna do?

00:35:04.640 --> 00:35:07.120
Never mind, I'm gonna educate that union

00:35:07.120 --> 00:35:09.800
real good to lay off us.

00:35:11.060 --> 00:35:12.680
Dad, are you gonna let me want to do?

00:35:12.800 --> 00:35:14.380
Give in to them, let the union take over?

00:35:14.520 --> 00:35:16.100
That's what'll happen once they grab hold.

00:35:17.340 --> 00:35:19.640
With their hours and benefits and guarantees,

00:35:19.820 --> 00:35:22.300
3% of the payroll for retirement, 2% for health,

00:35:22.420 --> 00:35:25.620
2% for vacations, always with a hand stuck out for more.

00:35:26.400 --> 00:35:28.220
